      "notes": "BOOT button — onboard bootloader-select pushbutton, also usable as a general input when application code is running. Not aliased in this board's pins_arduino.h (no PIN_BUTTON define shipped by arduino-pico for this board) — added directly as a chipGpios entry; raw pin number 21 is still usable via pinMode()/digitalRead() on arduino-pico. Confirmed via CircuitPython's pins.c for this board (MP_QSTR_BUTTON -> pin_GPIO21) and Adafruit's own pinouts guide (\"This button is also usable as an input in code, on pin board.BUTTON\")."
